  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "If a user is present in an invite only instance (and they are not the instance creator), they are able to vrchat.com: click on the instance they are currently in, and share the invite short link. \nAny user with that link can then click \"invite me\" to invite themselves, effectively making all instance privacy modes moot, so long as you have an \"insider\".\nWhile it's wildly convenient in other modes, it has potential for abuse - and users are typically in an invite only world because they want to control the flow of inbound users to prevent bad actors, or they're running an exclusive event with a \"leader\".\nI hope this is addressed prior to the implementation of any guild system.",
